    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25121" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάλειμμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαλείπω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>interstice, gap,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				59b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>PA</u>
				680b34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				12.31
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; in Music, <i>interval,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				921b10
			</span></i>; of Time, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.66.2
			</span></i>; <i>pause,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δ. τῆς ἐνεργείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Comp.</u>
					20
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ διαλειμμάτων</span> at
				<i>intervals,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				3p.64U.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Per.</u>
				7
			</span></i>; esp. of <i>intervals</i> between attacks of fever, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				7.414
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				427
			</span></i>.</div>
